# The trial of pod-iroh in podssh (T-810), at podssh's main 0370b0b
# (pod-iroh.commit). crates/podssh-iroh leaves podssh, with its tests, its
# four plants and podssh's copy of iroh-relay: podssh-cli takes pod-iroh
# with its feature iroh, and its iroh_way.rs gives the crate podssh's TLS
# context, resolver, proxy of the environment and way out
# (podssh_ws::client::way), and the values of PODSSH_IROH_*, which it reads
# by name (a test compares the names with pod-iroh's). podssh's root
# [patch.crates-io] names the fork of iroh-relay at podcrates' tag; the
# scan of the patches takes that git source. Each podcrates tag moves to
# v0.65.0. The repository checks; no file of the crate stays; no manifest
# names it; the build and clippy of the CLI with the feature, with the
# lints that the gate allows; pod-iroh and the fork in its tree; the tests
# of its library with the feature; the tests of the command line that the
# gate's step iroh runs with the relay and the server of pkarr on the
# loopback (feature iroh-test), each offline; the format; the toolchains
# and the test targets of the gate; the static binary with the feature, for
# x86_64 musl with zig.
python3 scripts/check-repo.py
test ! -e crates/podssh-iroh && test ! -e vendor/iroh-relay
! grep -rn --include=Cargo.toml --exclude-dir=target -e 'podssh-iroh' .
grep -q "^iroh-relay = { path = \"$PODCRATES/vendor/iroh-relay\" }" Cargo.toml
cargo build -q -p podssh-cli --features iroh
cargo tree -q -p podssh-cli --features iroh -i pod-iroh | grep -q '^pod-iroh v'
cargo tree -q -p podssh-cli --features iroh -i iroh-relay | grep -q "^iroh-relay v.*($PODCRATES/vendor/iroh-relay)"
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podssh-cli --features iroh -- -D warnings -A clippy::collapsible_if
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podssh-cli --features iroh-test -- -D warnings -A clippy::collapsible_if
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --features iroh --lib
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --features iroh-test --test iroh_road --test iroh_cli --test chat_iroh --test pipe_iroh --test pipe_iroh_record --test pinggy_road --test opentunnel_road --test man_page
cargo fmt -p podssh-cli --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-tests.py"
cargo zigbuild -q --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -p podssh-cli --bin podssh --features iroh
sh scripts/check-static.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podssh"
